#!/bin/bash
# Run the IRIX desktop session (/var/X11/xdm/Xsession.dt: 4Dwm, toolchest,
# fm -b, ...) on an X server with no window manager, as an X client for
# startx or a display manager:
#
#   startx /usr/QuickTransit/bin/irix-desktop -- :0
#
# Starts rpcbind and fam if needed.  Returns at toolchest Desktop > Log Out,
# which ends a startx session.
pgrep -x rpcbind >/dev/null || rpcbind
# fam (RPC program 391002).  rpcbind keeps the registration of a fam that
# was killed, so look for the process and drop a stale registration.
if ! pgrep -f '^/usr/QuickTransit/bin/QuickTransit .*/irix/usr/etc/fam( |$)' >/dev/null; then
    rpcinfo -d 391002 2 2>/dev/null
    setsid /irix/usr/etc/fam -f </dev/null >/dev/null 2>&1 &
    for i in $(seq 20); do
        rpcinfo -p localhost 2>/dev/null | grep -q sgi_fam && break
        sleep 0.5
    done
fi

export HOME=${HOME:-/root} USER=${USER:-root} LOGNAME=${LOGNAME:-root} SHELL=/bin/sh
cd "$HOME" || exit 1
# Xsession.dt starts everything in the background and ends with
# "exec reaper", which sets _SGI_SESSION_PROPERTY on the root window and
# exits.  Log Out (endsession) removes it; IRIX xdm then ends the session,
# and so does this script.
/irix/bin/sh /var/X11/xdm/Xsession.dt </dev/null
/irix/bin/sh -c '/usr/bin/X11/xprop -root -exists _SGI_SESSION_PROPERTY' >/dev/null

# Like xdm, end what the session left behind (fmserv outlives the X server).
# fam stays: it serves every display.
for p in $(pgrep -f '^/usr/QuickTransit/bin/QuickTransit '); do
    case "$(tr '\0' ' ' < /proc/$p/cmdline 2>/dev/null)" in
        *' /irix/usr/etc/fam '*) continue ;;
    esac
    tr '\0' '\n' < /proc/$p/environ 2>/dev/null | grep -qxF "DISPLAY=$DISPLAY" && kill $p
done
